Done. Three files in the module:

**`cache.go`** — LRU cache using `container/list` + `map[string]*list.Element`. `sync.RWMutex` for concurrency safety. Constructor returns error on `Capacity <= 0`. `Get`/`Put` both promote the accessed key to MRU (front of list). Full-cache `Put` evicts the back of the list.

**`cache_test.go`** — 9 tests covering:
- Invalid capacity rejection
- Basic Put/Get / Get miss
- Update existing key (value + MRU promotion)
- Get-on-hit and Put-update both mark MRU
- Eviction
- Len tracking through insert/update/eviction
- Concurrent safety

Benchmarks:
- `BenchmarkGet` — 100M ops at ~10.6 ns/op (hit in warm cache)
- `BenchmarkPutEviction` — 135M ops at ~8.8 ns/op (Put into full single-slot cache)

**`go.mod`** — `module example.helios/cache`, Go 1.26. No third-party dependencies.
